# Datalog

The least model of a Datalog program — ground facts and function-free Horn rules, with negation over lower strata —
computed semi-naively in pure LOGOS and compiled through every execution tier. Auto-imported on reference.

A program is a `Seq of DatalogFact` and a `Seq of DatalogRule`. `datalogEvaluate` answers a `DatalogModel` holding
every fact of the stratified least model, each once, the given facts first and every derived fact after the facts it
was derived from; or a `DatalogRefusal` saying why the program has none, in the words `logicaffeine_proof::datalog`
refuses it with: a predicate used with two arities, a variable of a rule's head or of a negated literal that no
positive literal binds, or predicates that depend on one another through a negation.

Evaluation is the textbook's. The predicates are ordered by the dependency graph (body predicate → head predicate):
a group of predicates that reach one another is evaluated as one stratum, after every stratum that reaches it, so a
negated literal only ever reads a relation already complete. Within a stratum each rule fires once over everything
known, and then, round after round, only on joins that read at least one fact the previous round derived — one
positive literal over those new facts, the others over all of them — until a round derives nothing.

## Note
A term of an atom: a variable its rule binds, or a constant.

## A DatalogTerm is either:
    A DatalogVar (name: Text).
    A DatalogConst (value: Text).

## Note
An atom `predicate(terms…)`.

## A DatalogAtom has:
    a predicate, which is Text.
    a terms, which is Seq of DatalogTerm.

## Note
A body literal: an atom that must hold, or one that must not (negation as failure, over a lower stratum).

## A DatalogLiteral is either:
    A DatalogPos (atom: DatalogAtom).
    A DatalogNeg (atom: DatalogAtom).

## Note
A rule `head :- body`, named for the facts it derives.

## A DatalogRule has:
    a name, which is Text.
    a head, which is DatalogAtom.
    a body, which is Seq of DatalogLiteral.

## Note
A ground fact `predicate(values…)`.

## A DatalogFact has:
    a predicate, which is Text.
    a values, which is Seq of Text.

## Note
What `datalogEvaluate` answers: the least model's facts, or why the program has no stratified least model.

## A DatalogOutcome is either:
    A DatalogModel (facts: Seq of DatalogFact).
    A DatalogRefusal (reason: Text).

## Note
The variable `name`.

## To datalogVar (name: Text) -> DatalogTerm:
    Return a new DatalogVar with name name.

## Note
The constant `value`.

## To datalogConst (value: Text) -> DatalogTerm:
    Return a new DatalogConst with value value.

## Note
The atom `predicate(terms…)`.

## To datalogAtom (predicate: Text) and (terms: Seq of DatalogTerm) -> DatalogAtom:
    Return a new DatalogAtom with predicate predicate and terms terms.

## Note
The literal that holds when `a` does.

## To datalogHolds (a: DatalogAtom) -> DatalogLiteral:
    Return a new DatalogPos with atom a.

## Note
The literal that holds when `a` does not.

## To datalogNot (a: DatalogAtom) -> DatalogLiteral:
    Return a new DatalogNeg with atom a.

## Note
The rule `name: head :- body`.

## To datalogRule (name: Text) and (head: DatalogAtom) and (body: Seq of DatalogLiteral) -> DatalogRule:
    Return a new DatalogRule with name name and head head and body body.

## Note
The fact `predicate(values…)`.

## To datalogFact (predicate: Text) and (values: Seq of Text) -> DatalogFact:
    Return a new DatalogFact with predicate predicate and values values.

## Note
True when the term is a variable.

## To datalogIsVar (t: DatalogTerm) -> Bool:
    Let mutable answer be false.
    Inspect t:
        When DatalogVar (v):
            Set answer to true.
        When DatalogConst (c):
            Set answer to false.
    Return answer.

## Note
A variable's name, or a constant's value.

## To datalogTermText (t: DatalogTerm) -> Text:
    Let mutable answer be "".
    Inspect t:
        When DatalogVar (v):
            Set answer to v.
        When DatalogConst (c):
            Set answer to c.
    Return answer.

## Note
The atom a literal asserts or denies.

## To datalogLiteralAtom (l: DatalogLiteral) -> DatalogAtom:
    Let mutable answer be a new DatalogAtom.
    Inspect l:
        When DatalogPos (a):
            Set answer to a.
        When DatalogNeg (a):
            Set answer to a.
    Return answer.

## Note
True when the literal denies its atom.

## To datalogIsNegated (l: DatalogLiteral) -> Bool:
    Let mutable answer be false.
    Inspect l:
        When DatalogPos (a):
            Set answer to false.
        When DatalogNeg (a):
            Set answer to true.
    Return answer.

## Note
The atoms of a rule's body that must hold (`negated` false) or must not (`negated` true), in body order.

## To datalogBodyAtoms (r: DatalogRule) and (negated: Bool) -> Seq of DatalogAtom:
    Let mutable atoms be a new Seq of DatalogAtom.
    Repeat for l in r's body:
        If datalogIsNegated(l) is equal to negated:
            Push datalogLiteralAtom(l) to atoms.
    Return atoms.

## Note
The text a fact's predicate and values are kept under: each as its length in bytes, a colon and its bytes, so two
different facts never share it whatever their values hold.

## To datalogKey (predicate: Text) and (values: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    Let n be length of text_bytes(predicate).
    Let mutable key be "{n}:{predicate}".
    Repeat for v in values:
        Let m be length of text_bytes(v).
        Set key to key + "{m}:{v}".
    Return key.

## Note
`predicate(values…)`, as the model is printed.

## To datalogShowFact (f: DatalogFact) -> Text:
    Let p be f's predicate.
    Let shown be join(f's values, ", ").
    Return "{p}({shown})".

## Note
The first predicate used with two arities — the facts' first, then each rule's head and body in order — as the
refusal names it, or "" when every predicate has one arity.

## To datalogArityClash (facts: Seq of DatalogFact) and (rules: Seq of DatalogRule) -> Text:
    Let mutable names be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable arities be a new Seq of Int.
    Repeat for f in facts:
        Push f's predicate to names.
        Push length of f's values to arities.
    Repeat for r in rules:
        Let h be r's head.
        Push h's predicate to names.
        Push length of h's terms to arities.
        Repeat for l in r's body:
            Let a be datalogLiteralAtom(l).
            Push a's predicate to names.
            Push length of a's terms to arities.
    Let mutable seen be a new Map of Text to Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most length of names:
        Let p be item i of names.
        Let found be item i of arities.
        If seen contains p:
            Let expected be item p of seen.
            If expected is not found:
                Return "`{p}` is used with {expected} arguments and with {found}".
        Otherwise:
            Set item p of seen to found.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return "".

## Note
The first rule with a variable in its head or in a negated literal that no positive literal binds, as the refusal
names it, or "" when every rule is safe.

## To datalogUnsafe (rules: Seq of DatalogRule) -> Text:
    Repeat for r in rules:
        Let mutable bound be a new Set of Text.
        Repeat for a in datalogBodyAtoms(r, false):
            Repeat for t in a's terms:
                If datalogIsVar(t):
                    Add datalogTermText(t) to bound.
        Let rule be r's name.
        Let negated be datalogBodyAtoms(r, true).
        Let mutable mustBind be a new Seq of DatalogAtom.
        Push r's head to mustBind.
        Repeat for a in negated:
            Push a to mustBind.
        Repeat for a in mustBind:
            Repeat for t in a's terms:
                If datalogIsVar(t):
                    Let v be datalogTermText(t).
                    If not (bound contains v):
                        Return "rule `{rule}`: `{v}` appears in no positive body literal, so nothing bounds it".
    Return "".

## Note
The predicates the rules name, each once, in the order the rules first name them: each rule's head, then its body.

## To datalogRulePredicates (rules: Seq of DatalogRule) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable preds be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable seen be a new Set of Text.
    Repeat for r in rules:
        Let h be r's head.
        Let p be h's predicate.
        If not (seen contains p):
            Add p to seen.
            Push p to preds.
        Repeat for l in r's body:
            Let a be datalogLiteralAtom(l).
            Let q be a's predicate.
            If not (seen contains q):
                Add q to seen.
                Push q to preds.
    Return preds.

## Note
Which predicate reaches which through one or more rules: entry `(i - 1) * n + j` is true when predicate `j` of `preds`
can be derived, through a chain of rules, from predicate `i`.

## To datalogReach (rules: Seq of DatalogRule) and (preds: Seq of Text) -> Seq of Bool:
    Let n be length of preds.
    Let mutable rank be a new Map of Text to Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Set item (item i of preds) of rank to i.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Let mutable reach be a new Seq of Bool.
    Let mutable k be 1.
    While k is at most n * n:
        Push false to reach.
        Set k to k + 1.
    Repeat for r in rules:
        Let h be item (r's head's predicate) of rank.
        Repeat for l in r's body:
            Let a be datalogLiteralAtom(l).
            Let b be item (a's predicate) of rank.
            Set item ((b - 1) * n + h) of reach to true.
    Let mutable via be 1.
    While via is at most n:
        Let mutable src be 1.
        While src is at most n:
            If item ((src - 1) * n + via) of reach:
                Let mutable dst be 1.
                While dst is at most n:
                    If item ((via - 1) * n + dst) of reach:
                        Set item ((src - 1) * n + dst) of reach to true.
                    Set dst to dst + 1.
            Set src to src + 1.
        Set via to via + 1.
    Return reach.

## Note
`names` in byte order.

## To datalogSortTexts (names: Seq of Text) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable ordered be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for x in names:
        Let mutable placed be a new Seq of Text.
        Let mutable done be false.
        Repeat for y in ordered:
            If not done:
                If compareText(x, y) is less than 0:
                    Push x to placed.
                    Set done to true.
            Push y to placed.
        If not done:
            Push x to placed.
        Set ordered to placed.
    Return ordered.

## Note
The first negation inside a cycle of the rules, which no stratum order can finish before it is read, as the refusal
names it: every predicate of that cycle, in byte order. "" when there is none.

## To datalogUnstratifiable (rules: Seq of DatalogRule) -> Text:
    Let preds be datalogRulePredicates(rules).
    Let n be length of preds.
    Let reach be datalogReach(rules, preds).
    Let mutable rank be a new Map of Text to Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Set item (item i of preds) of rank to i.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Repeat for r in rules:
        Let h be item (r's head's predicate) of rank.
        Repeat for a in datalogBodyAtoms(r, true):
            Let q be item (a's predicate) of rank.
            Let together be (q is equal to h) or (item ((q - 1) * n + h) of reach and item ((h - 1) * n + q) of reach).
            If together:
                Let mutable cycle be a new Seq of Text.
                Let mutable m be 1.
                While m is at most n:
                    If (m is equal to h) or (item ((m - 1) * n + h) of reach and item ((h - 1) * n + m) of reach):
                        Push item m of preds to cycle.
                    Set m to m + 1.
                Let names be join(datalogSortTexts(cycle), ", ").
                Return "{names} depend on one another through a negation".
    Return "".

## Note
The least model of `facts` and `rules`, or why they have none.

## To datalogEvaluate (facts: Seq of DatalogFact) and (rules: Seq of DatalogRule) -> DatalogOutcome:
    Let arity be datalogArityClash(facts, rules).
    If arity is not "":
        Return a new DatalogRefusal with reason arity.
    Let unbound be datalogUnsafe(rules).
    If unbound is not "":
        Return a new DatalogRefusal with reason unbound.
    Let cyclic be datalogUnstratifiable(rules).
    If cyclic is not "":
        Return a new DatalogRefusal with reason cyclic.
    Let rulePreds be datalogRulePredicates(rules).
    Let n be length of rulePreds.
    Let reach be datalogReach(rules, rulePreds).
    Let mutable rank be a new Map of Text to Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Set item (item i of rulePreds) of rank to i.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Let mutable preds be copy of rulePreds.
    Repeat for f in facts:
        Let p be f's predicate.
        If not (rank contains p):
            Push p to preds.
            Set item p of rank to length of preds.
    Let np be length of preds.
    Let mutable keys be a new Set of Text.
    Let mutable factPred be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable factStart be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable factValues be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for f in facts:
        Let key be datalogKey(f's predicate, f's values).
        If not (keys contains key):
            Add key to keys.
            Push item (f's predicate) of rank to factPred.
            Push length of factValues + 1 to factStart.
            Repeat for v in f's values:
                Push v to factValues.
    Let mutable earlier be a new Seq of Int.
    Set i to 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Let mutable before be 0.
        Let mutable j be 1.
        While j is at most n:
            If item ((j - 1) * n + i) of reach and not item ((i - 1) * n + j) of reach:
                Set before to before + 1.
            Set j to j + 1.
        Push before to earlier.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Let mutable level be 0.
    While level is less than n:
        Let mutable stratum be a new Seq of DatalogRule.
        Repeat for r in rules:
            If item (item (r's head's predicate) of rank) of earlier is equal to level:
                Push r to stratum.
        Let mutable deltaFrom be 0.
        Let mutable more be length of stratum is greater than 0.
        While more:
            Let total be length of factPred.
            Let roundStart be total + 1.
            Let mutable blockStart be a new Seq of Int.
            Let mutable old be a new Seq of Int.
            Let mutable sizes be a new Seq of Int.
            Let mutable p be 1.
            While p is at most np:
                Push 0 to sizes.
                Push 0 to old.
                Set p to p + 1.
            Let mutable f be 1.
            While f is at most total:
                Let fp be item f of factPred.
                Set item fp of sizes to item fp of sizes + 1.
                If f is less than deltaFrom:
                    Set item fp of old to item fp of old + 1.
                Set f to f + 1.
            Push 1 to blockStart.
            Set p to 1.
            While p is at most np:
                Push item p of blockStart + item p of sizes to blockStart.
                Set p to p + 1.
            Let mutable cursor be copy of blockStart.
            Let mutable order be a new Seq of Int.
            Set f to 1.
            While f is at most total:
                Push 0 to order.
                Set f to f + 1.
            Set f to 1.
            While f is at most total:
                Let fp be item f of factPred.
                Let slot be item fp of cursor.
                Set item slot of order to f.
                Set item fp of cursor to item fp of cursor + 1.
                Set f to f + 1.
            Repeat for r in stratum:
                Let positive be datalogBodyAtoms(r, false).
                Let negative be datalogBodyAtoms(r, true).
                Let mutable vars be a new Seq of Text.
                Repeat for a in positive:
                    Repeat for t in a's terms:
                        If datalogIsVar(t) and not (vars contains datalogTermText(t)):
                            Push datalogTermText(t) to vars.
                Let nv be length of vars.
                Let mutable firing be 0.
                Let mutable last be 0.
                If deltaFrom is greater than 0:
                    Set firing to 1.
                    Set last to length of positive.
                While firing is at most last:
                    Let mutable live be true.
                    If firing is greater than 0:
                        Let fired be item firing of positive.
                        Let dp be item (fired's predicate) of rank.
                        Set live to item dp of sizes is greater than item dp of old.
                    If live:
                        Let mutable rows be a new Seq of Text.
                        Let mutable rowCount be 1.
                        Let mutable k be 1.
                        While k is at most nv:
                            Push "" to rows.
                            Set k to k + 1.
                        Let mutable bound be a new Seq of Bool.
                        Set k to 1.
                        While k is at most nv:
                            Push false to bound.
                            Set k to k + 1.
                        Let mutable j be 1.
                        While j is at most length of positive:
                            Let a be item j of positive.
                            Let ap be item (a's predicate) of rank.
                            Let mutable lo be item ap of blockStart.
                            If j is equal to firing:
                                Set lo to lo + item ap of old.
                            Let hi be item (ap + 1) of blockStart - 1.
                            Let width be length of a's terms.
                            Let mutable slots be a new Seq of Int.
                            Repeat for t in a's terms:
                                If datalogIsVar(t):
                                    Let name be datalogTermText(t).
                                    Let mutable s be 1.
                                    While item s of vars is not name:
                                        Set s to s + 1.
                                    Push s to slots.
                                Otherwise:
                                    Push 0 to slots.
                            Let mutable nextRows be a new Seq of Text.
                            Let mutable nextCount be 0.
                            Let mutable joined be 0.
                            While joined is less than rowCount:
                                Let mutable c be lo.
                                While c is at most hi:
                                    Let fact be item c of order.
                                    Let base be item fact of factStart.
                                    Let mutable cand be a new Seq of Text.
                                    Let mutable known be copy of bound.
                                    Set k to 1.
                                    While k is at most nv:
                                        Push item (joined * nv + k) of rows to cand.
                                        Set k to k + 1.
                                    Let mutable ok be true.
                                    Let mutable t be 1.
                                    While ok and t is at most width:
                                        Let v be item (base + t - 1) of factValues.
                                        Let s be item t of slots.
                                        If s is equal to 0:
                                            If datalogTermText(item t of a's terms) is not v:
                                                Set ok to false.
                                        Otherwise:
                                            If item s of known:
                                                If item s of cand is not v:
                                                    Set ok to false.
                                            Otherwise:
                                                Set item s of cand to v.
                                                Set item s of known to true.
                                        Set t to t + 1.
                                    If ok:
                                        Repeat for v in cand:
                                            Push v to nextRows.
                                        Set nextCount to nextCount + 1.
                                    Set c to c + 1.
                                Set joined to joined + 1.
                            Repeat for s in slots:
                                If s is greater than 0:
                                    Set item s of bound to true.
                            Set rows to nextRows.
                            Set rowCount to nextCount.
                            Set j to j + 1.
                        Let mutable row be 0.
                        While row is less than rowCount:
                            Let mutable holds be true.
                            Repeat for a in negative:
                                Let mutable denied be a new Seq of Text.
                                Repeat for t in a's terms:
                                    If datalogIsVar(t):
                                        Let name be datalogTermText(t).
                                        Let mutable s be 1.
                                        While item s of vars is not name:
                                            Set s to s + 1.
                                        Push item (row * nv + s) of rows to denied.
                                    Otherwise:
                                        Push datalogTermText(t) to denied.
                                If keys contains datalogKey(a's predicate, denied):
                                    Set holds to false.
                            If holds:
                                Let h be r's head.
                                Let mutable derived be a new Seq of Text.
                                Repeat for t in h's terms:
                                    If datalogIsVar(t):
                                        Let name be datalogTermText(t).
                                        Let mutable s be 1.
                                        While item s of vars is not name:
                                            Set s to s + 1.
                                        Push item (row * nv + s) of rows to derived.
                                    Otherwise:
                                        Push datalogTermText(t) to derived.
                                Let key be datalogKey(h's predicate, derived).
                                If not (keys contains key):
                                    Add key to keys.
                                    Push item (h's predicate) of rank to factPred.
                                    Push length of factValues + 1 to factStart.
                                    Repeat for v in derived:
                                        Push v to factValues.
                            Set row to row + 1.
                    Set firing to firing + 1.
            Set deltaFrom to roundStart.
            Set more to length of factPred is at least roundStart.
        Set level to level + 1.
    Let mutable model be a new Seq of DatalogFact.
    Let stored be length of factPred.
    Let mutable g be 1.
    While g is at most stored:
        Let mutable vs be a new Seq of Text.
        Let mutable past be length of factValues + 1.
        If g is less than stored:
            Set past to item (g + 1) of factStart.
        Let mutable k be item g of factStart.
        While k is less than past:
            Push item k of factValues to vs.
            Set k to k + 1.
        Let name be item (item g of factPred) of preds.
        Let fact be a new DatalogFact with predicate name and values vs.
        Push fact to model.
        Set g to g + 1.
    Return a new DatalogModel with facts model.
